The following files are derived from that project, based on its v1.4.0
release:

  backend/    ui/    design/    config/    test/
  gui.py      requirements.txt

Modifications made by this repository, and not present upstream:

  setup_cuda_env.py          builds an embedded Python 3.12.10 environment
                             with CUDA-enabled torch, so the v1.4.0 sources
                             run on an NVIDIA GPU on Windows.
  start_official_cuda.bat    launcher for that embedded environment.
  README.md                  rewritten installation and usage notes.

The upstream v1.4.0 release ships a CPU-only installer, with CUDA left
disabled in its requirements. The upstream source already contains the
device detection for CUDA. These modifications therefore do not add new
GPU code paths; they restore the ability to use the ones already present.

